      "side": 1,
      "message": "Acknowledged regarding `bug_0_length_line.pdf`. This difference is indeed caused by removing the legacy hack:\n\n```C++\nif (dash_len \u003c\u003d 0.000001f) { dash_len \u003d 0.1f; }\n```\nThe old code artificially rendered 0-length dashes as 0.1-length segments.  I restore this specific clamping logic (for 0-length dashes) to preserve backward compatibility.",
      "parentUuid": "2f3c391f_bc53ff5b",
      "revId": "830f56bac14357fd479cdb47f346e70bfb2907f8",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
